  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Hello!\nI play VRChat on my laptop, due to me unable to get a headset at this time, and since the Unity 2019 update and then on VRC has been crashing randomly and sometimes causing my laptop to back screen making it usable until I hit the power key to turn it off.\nAt the beginning it was only crashing here and there but now its every time I first get on it takes around 30 minutes to crash/black screen the first time. Then after, it will do it again and again after minutes of me rejoining my friends. \nThe game runs perfectly fine, no frame drops or ping problems, just like it would before it ever started crashing/black screening randomly. I have checked my steam files, deleted and reinstalled VRChat, deleted my cache, made sure my computer is up to date, and even deleted then reinstalled windows but nothing seems to be working. \nI might be missing something small or something I'm just not seeing, but everything I have done hasn't worked. Is there anything I can do to fix this or do I have to wait until I get a new PC for me to even run the game properly again?\nThank you!",
